  a closed `t:class/0`, and the Chatman failure-taxonomy `broken_term` the refusal
  witnesses. GraphLaw derives and validates; it never authorizes, so a refusal
  never grants or withdraws authority.

  `:raw` keeps the whole engine error map exactly as decoded (lossless, so fields this
  library does not know are never dropped); it is `nil` for client-side refusals built
  with `new/3`, `build/3` or a per-code constructor.

